window.docContents[151].resolve({"/Tactics/#Logical-Foundations--Tactics___-More-Basic-Tactics--Using--cases--on-Expressions":{"contents":"\n\nThe cases tactic can be used on expressions as well as\nvariables:\n\ndef chooseIf {α : Type} (test : α → Bool) (x y : α) : α :=\n  if test x then x else y\n\ntheorem chooseIf_self {α : Type} (test : α → Bool) (x : α) :\n    chooseIf test x x = x := by\n  rw [chooseIf]\n  cases test x <;> rfl\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n","context":"Logical Foundations\u0009Tactics: More Basic Tactics","header":"7.7. Using  cases  on Expressions","id":"/Tactics/#Logical-Foundations--Tactics___-More-Basic-Tactics--Using--cases--on-Expressions"}});